# level_climax.vmus: level 7, docs/design/audio.md Music.
# Original composition for this project. Mood: fast, both motifs layered:
# the title's pentatonic "Egyptian" motif (D A G A C A, D E G A C) on the
# lead and harp, over the dog-tech idiom of level_dt (driving 50% square bass
# riff, noise snare, metallic clanks, steam).
# Channels: 0 lead / stabs, 1 harp 16ths / metal, 2 square bass, 3 drums.
# Tempo 3: 4 rows per beat = 175 BPM, one pattern = 64 x 3 / 35 = 5.49 s.
# Generated once with a throwaway script and edited by hand from here on.
vmus 1
tempo 3

inst 01 square   vol=36 a=0 d=6 s=40 r=4 duty=64    # lead, 25% duty
inst 02 square   vol=50 a=0 d=6 s=36 r=2 duty=128   # dog-tech bass, 50% duty
inst 03 triangle vol=64 a=0 d=5 s=0                 # kick: pitch drops with D7f
inst 04 noise    vol=28 a=0 d=1 s=0                 # hat
inst 05 noise    vol=56 a=0 d=6 s=0                 # snare
inst 06 noise    vol=44 a=0 d=4 s=0 mode=1          # anvil clank (metallic)
inst 07 pluck    vol=60 a=0 d=0 s=64 r=8 damp=248   # harp pluck
inst 08 square   vol=28 a=0 d=3 s=0 duty=32         # thin stab, arpeggiated
inst 09 noise    vol=30 a=8 d=24 s=0 mode=1         # steam release
inst 0a pluck    vol=60 a=0 d=0 s=64 r=16 damp=256  # long harp (break)

